{"text": "W", "etymologies": [{"etymologyHTML": "<p>W (<i>upper case</i>, <i>lower case</i> <b class=\"Latn\" lang=\"en\">w</b>, <i>plural</i> <b class=\"Latn\" lang=\"en\">Ws</b> <i>or</i> <b class=\"Latn\" lang=\"en\">W's</b>)\n</p>", "pos": []}, {"etymologyHTML": "<p>Abbreviations of various words beginning with W.\n</p>", "pos": [{"pos": "Noun", "definitions": [{"definition": "Abbreviation of women (sign on toilet door).\n\n", "quote": [{"citation": "2001, Jonathan Franzen, The Corrections, New York, NY: Farrar, Straus and Giroux, \u2192ISBN, page 332:", "text": "From the Kierkegaard Room he lopingly careened through a red-carpeted hallway that had previously vouchsafed him a comfort station but this morning seemed all business, no M or W in sight, just salons and boutiques and the Ingmar Bergman Cinema."}], "relative": {"Coordinate term": ["M (\u201cmen\u201d)"]}}, {"definition": "(uncountable) Abbreviation of west.\n", "quote": [], "relative": {"Coordinate terms": ["E (\u201ceast\u201d)", "N (\u201cnorth\u201d)", "S (\u201csouth\u201d)"]}}, {"definition": "Abbreviation of Wednesday.\n", "quote": [], "relative": {"Synonyms": ["Wed", "Wed."], "Coordinate terms": ["Su", "M", "Tu", "Th", "F", "Sa"]}}, {"definition": " (sports) Abbreviation of wins (statistic).\n", "quote": [], "relative": {"Coordinate terms": ["L (\u201closses\u201d)", "T (\u201cties\u201d)"]}}, {"definition": " (countable, Internet slang) Abbreviation of win.\n", "quote": [], "relative": {"Coordinate term": ["L (\u201closs\u201d)"]}}, {"definition": "(cricket) Abbreviation of wicket.", "quote": [], "relative": {}}, {"definition": "(law enforcement) Abbreviation of warrant.", "quote": [], "relative": {}}]}, {"pos": "Adjective", "definitions": [{"definition": "(slang) Excellent, top-notch (abbreviation of winner). (Compare noun sense 4 and sense 5.)\n", "quote": [], "relative": {"Antonym": ["L (\u201cbad", "subpar\u201d)"]}}]}, {"pos": "Noun", "definitions": [{"definition": "(stenoscript) Abbreviation of week.", "quote": [], "relative": {}}, {"definition": "(stenoscript) Abbreviation of west.", "quote": [], "relative": {}}]}]}], "pronunciation": [["US, abbreviation, rare, nonstandard", "/\u02c8d\u028cb/"], ["US", "/\u02c8d\u028cb\u0259(l)ju/"], ["UK", "/\u02c8d\u028cb(\u0259l)ju\u02d0/"]]}